      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily comes to 15 g/day. That is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day, and a single 5 g dose is already in the range where acute liver injury is a concern. A 70 kg patient with normal liver function is still at risk at that dose. It could cause serious hepatotoxicity.\n\nWas this a typo? Here are some common regimens I could enter instead:\n- **650 mg PO, 4 times daily** (2,600 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO, 3 times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO, 4 times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the standard maximum). Many institutions cap at 3 g/day for some patients.\n\nIf you meant a different dose or frequency, tell me and I'll enter it. If you really do intend the original dose, for example as part of a protocol I don't know about, it needs to go through pharmacy and your institution's override process. I shouldn't enter it directly."
      }
     ],
