      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen at 15 g/day carries a high risk of acute liver failure, and that risk doesn't depend on who orders it. I don't know of any clinical indication that would make this dose appropriate.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a safe dose right away.** For example, acetaminophen 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day). I can add a note with the max daily dose.\n- **Support a pharmacy review.** If you think there's a protocol I'm not aware of, pharmacy and the medication safety team can review it. I can help you write up the request.\n- **Look at the underlying goal.** If the goal is stronger analgesia or fever control, I can enter an alternative or adjunct that fits your plan.\n\nTell me which you'd like, and I'll do it."
      }
     ],
